From: Korri contributors
Subject: [PATCH] rendervulkan: compile pipelines on demand only

BInit() started a detached gamescope-shdr thread that compiled every
pipeline variant. Its keys do not match the ones composition asks for
(for example, BLIT with blur_layers 1 against 0 at runtime), so the
work is never used. pipeline() already compiles a missing variant on
first use. On an RG353M (Mali-G52, panvk) the thread held one core at
about 100% for over a minute after start.

Do not start the thread.

Korri-local; not upstream.

Rebased onto 3.16.31: the thread is now a std::jthread member with a
stop token (389e7e2c). Leave m_pipelineThread default-constructed. It
is not joinable, so its stop and join at exit do nothing. This also
skips the new SGSR type; pipeline() compiles it on first use, as it
does EASU and NIS.
---
 src/rendervulkan.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/rendervulkan.cpp b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
index 11ce4e88..87a83596 100644
--- a/src/rendervulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
@@ -323,7 +323,8 @@ bool CVulkanDevice::BInit(VkInstance instance, VkSurfaceKHR surface)
 
 	m_bInitialized = true;
 
-	m_pipelineThread = std::jthread([this](std::stop_token st){compileAllPipelines(st);});
+	// No compileAllPipelines(): its keys miss runtime keys, pipeline() compiles on demand, and it costs a full core for over a minute on slow GPUs.
+	// m_pipelineThread stays default-constructed (not joinable), so its stop/join at exit does nothing.
 
 	g_reshadeManager.init(this);
 
